WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>The Company Commander's
Triumphant Return</b>

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.330
Congratulations!

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.990
We wish you all the best!

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.520
<b>Hermina (16)
Berthold's wife</b>

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:45.280
Please stop for a moment.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.060
Whoa.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.020
Congratulations, sir!

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:50.430
Congratulations!

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:52.850
Congratulations on your wedding.

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:53.760
Congratulations.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.290
Congratulations, Berthold-san.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.570
Well, thank you.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.800
<b>Berthold (32)
 Company Commander of 
Aitheria Palace Guards aka "the Devil"</b>

00:00:58.570 --> 00:00:59.800
Thank you to all of you.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.670
<b>Nikolaus (24)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.670
<b>Hans (23)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.670
Wow, that is a huge dowry!

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.690
Right?

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:07.540
It seems my father went all out on this.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.530
He's that squid fisherman, right?

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.050
And your wife is beautiful, too!

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:14.830
Can't say I'm not envious, sir!

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:19.850
I'm the happiest man on Earth!

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.450
I'm the most miserable man on Earth.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.350
Here you go, Hermina-san.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.100
Thank you so much.

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:29.580
What happened?

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:32.230
You looked so happy this morning.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:37.830
The previous tenant is still living 
in the Hermina's and my new home,

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.470
so we can't move in yet.

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:42.210
Apparently a traveling clergyman 
forcefully borrowed the

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:45.280
the carriage that the tenant 
was going to use for the move.

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:49.090
I can't just leave that dowry outside,

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:51.850
so I stuffed it into the officer 
barracks that I used to live in.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.230
But now we don't have a place to live.

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:57.950
All this when Hermina is already anxious

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:01.500
after coming to a place where
she doesn't know anybody or anything.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:06.660
I can't even provide her with a 
place she feels comfortable in!

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.860
Could I be any more useless 
of a man than this?

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:12.540
Which brings me to...

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:13.230
Yes?

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:17.520
I was wondering if Hermina 
could work here for a while.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:18.420
Huh?

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:21.750
We have an inn reserved for the 
nights, so nights are not a problem.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:26.290
But I'd like to provide her a 
place to stay while I'm at work.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:30.960
Actually, we are incredibly busy right now,

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:35.630
but we'd hate to impose 
on a newlywed bride.

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:38.130
Meaning, we'd love to have 
any help we can get!

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:38.140
<b>Eva (14)
Dishwasher at Nobu.
Resident of Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:40.130
We'd be so grateful.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.240
We were actually getting 
really desperate for help.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:47.380
I can only help with simple 
tasks, but thank you very much!

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:48.640
Thank you so much!

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:51.480
What was that?

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.050
Th-That was...

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:54.420
Wait!

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:09.860
Hermina-san, that was incredible!

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:11.520
You're not scared of eel?

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.450
I am a fisherman's daughter after all.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:17.260
Are you all right, Berthold-san?

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:18.450
Phew!

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:21.900
This reminds me. Nikolaus 
and Hans were telling me

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:24.880
that eel had become popular in 
Aitheria while I was away.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:27.820
That eel is actually why we're so busy.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:28.420
Huh?

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:32.910
Well, having him try it is probably 
faster than explaining it.

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:37.930
<b>Sizzle</b>

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.270
<b>Eel Kabayaki</b>

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.270
<b>What most people think of when 
they hear the word "unagi."
 Enjoy this dish with its special sauce.</b>

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:42.250
This is eel kabayaki.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:47.090
This is indeed unlike any 
eel dish I've seen before.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:49.390
But I mean, this is eel we're talking about.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:57.010
Wow, this eel is delicious!

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:57.020
<b>Fluffy</b>

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:57.020
<b>Melt</b>

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:58.670
It is?

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:07.130
<b>Melt</b>

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:07.130
<b>Soft</b>

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:07.140
This is completely different 
from the eel we're used to.

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:09.750
The difference is in the preparation.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.460
Try this too.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:12.390
It's called umaki.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:17.670
<b>Umaki</b>

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:17.670
<b>This eel wrapped in layers of egg 
is so good it'll force you to smile</b>

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:13.920
Umaki?

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.140
It's the same eel wrapped in layers of egg.

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:20.190
Let's try this, Berthold-san.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:21.050
Let's do that.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:30.250
<b>Melt</b>

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:30.250
<b>Soft</b>

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:30.430
The rich flavor of unagi 
delicately wrapped up in egg!

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:36.320
The strong kabayaki flavor and 
soft egg are a perfect match.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:39.320
You can have the last piece, Hermina.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:43.020
Then let's do this and 
each have half a piece.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:48.050
Thank you so much!

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.420
That was wonderful.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:50.110
Thank you.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:53.200
Taishou's eel is the best.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:57.210
I can see how this would 
make your store more busy.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:01.800
You don't look too happy about this.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:03.360
That's not true.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:07.080
The problem is that everyone's 
only ordering eel right now.

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:11.710
It takes a long time to prepare the eel, 
so when the customers only want that,

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.600
we have to keep them waiting

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:16.360
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:18.090
At this rate, we're no longer "Izakaya 
Nobu" but more like "Unagiya Nobu."

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:18.100
<b>Unagiya Nobu</b>

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:23.590
Worst of all is that customers who come 
to enjoy a drink can't even get in.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:25.560
Hmm, what's this scent?

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:26.600
Smells like eel.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:28.020
Lorenz-san.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:39.880
<b>Sake</b>

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.220
What brings you here?

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.170
I came here to ask you for a favor,

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:35.280
but this scent has completely bewitched me!

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:38.370
We were about to sit down 
and have our employee meal.

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:39.870
Care to join us?

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:43.250
<b>Unadon</b>

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:43.250
<b>The sauce is what makes this eel rice bowl.
 Even just rice with this sauce is amazing.</b>

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:44.730
Wow, eel for lunch? Lucky!

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:47.760
<b>Lorenz (50)
Glass Craft Guild Meister</b>

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:47.760
So this is rice with eel on top.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:51.680
This sheen is truly drawing me in.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:55.750
<i>This is—</i>

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:03.710
This eel is amazing!

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:07.140
I've never had this before, but it 
really goes well with the rice, too.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.390
I love the bold sauce!

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:12.290
I could just eat the sauce-soaked rice.

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:15.760
Having unadon for our employee 
lunch is so amazing.

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:20.020
The reminds me. What about the 
favor you were talking about?

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:22.500
Oh, yes.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:26.930
I've got a whole mountain 
of these little boxes

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:30.040
the wood-cutter guild's 
apprentices made for practice.

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:32.520
I was wondering if you'd 
have any use for them?

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.670
I could use one or two maybe, 
but not more than that.

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:39.670
How lucky is it that we get to 
have this delicacy at lunch?

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:42.740
We won't be having unadon every day,

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:45.230
but our meals are always dishes 
that Taishou is proud of,

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:46.940
so you can expect something good.

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:48.990
Thank you.

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:50.010
But...

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.330
What's wrong, Hermina?

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.790
It's not right that only I am 
having such a wonderful lunch.

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:57.830
If only I could bring this 
lunch to you somehow...

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:00.570
Oh you. Don't be ridiculous.

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:02.410
Taishou!

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:04.530
I just realized, too.

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:13.810
<b>Nobu's Special
Eel Bento</b>

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:11.720
Three eel bentos please!

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:13.810
Then I'll take another, too.

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:15.510
Here you go, two.

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:17.270
And you had three.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:18.560
Two for me.

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:20.150
Thank you very much!

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:21.700
Here you go, your change.

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:23.170
Three eel bentos please!

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:25.230
Coming right up. One moment please.

00:07:25.230 --> 00:07:26.560
Next please!

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:29.400
We've got more here.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:30.820
These are selling so fast!

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:40.070
These so-called bento lunch 
boxes are so clever.

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:44.710
<b>Nobu's Special Eel Bento</b>

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:44.710
<b>A tiny bit of a luxury for lunch...</b>

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:44.710
Oh ,here it is!

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:51.630
There's a few other stores now 
trying to sell something similar,

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:53.720
but the texture of this unagi...

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:59.730
That's not something anyone can replicate.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:02.390
No, the same goes for this sauce, too!

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:05.790
Once you've tasted Nobu, 
you can't go anywhere else.

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:09.210
Damn that Nobu.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:12.390
How dare they sell eel bentos when 
they won't sell Napolitan bentos?

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:13.370
An outrage!

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:17.380
<b>Gernot (37)
 Tax Collector
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:17.600
A complete outrage!

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:22.630
I was able to take care of the wooden 
boxes, and I got tasty lunches.

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:25.980
I'm grateful.

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:29.750
I didn't know eel could 
be prepared this way!

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:32.450
That's right! I'm convinced this is going

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:35.640
to become Aitheria's new big business.

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:38.920
So lucky that you got those rights for free.

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:41.820
This really is addictive though.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:44.640
These eels were fished 
from our waters, right,

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:45.760
Reinhold-san?

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:46.770
Huh? Well...

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:49.500
That was two eel bentos, right?

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:53.010
Is Hermina able to help out at all?

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.030
She is!

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:57.920
She calculates quickly and 
the customers love her.

00:08:58.340 --> 00:08:59.700
They love her?

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:03.470
This is your portion, Berthold-san.

00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:04.860
Oh.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:06.960
Hermina-san made it herself.

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:08.530
Really?

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:13.660
But she forgot the all-important eel!

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:17.030
Why don't you start eating it to check?

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:22.520
Oh! This is...

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:24.030
We call this mamushi.

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:25.290
Mamushi?

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:28.110
Yes. For this, the eel 
is steamed inside rice.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:35.190
That's delicious!

00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:38.960
No matter how many times I try it, 
your eel really is the best, Taishou.

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:42.330
That's not a nice thing 
to say to Hermina-san.

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:44.670
You mean Hermina grilled this?

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:47.130
Here's your change.

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:48.330
Thank you so much.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:51.070
She tried her best, but 
the flesh fell apart.

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:53.010
So that's why it's a mamushi.

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:58.660
<b>Shijimi no Akadashi</b>

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:58.660
<b>Delicious basket clams in miso soup.
 It's best when made with red miso.</b>

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:56.060
Here's some shijimi soup.

00:09:56.060 --> 00:09:58.680
Hermina-san made this too.

00:09:59.020 --> 00:10:00.320
This one, right?

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:01.950
I'd like three, too!

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:04.580
This is such a luxury.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:03.510
Yes, sir.

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:05.510
Could I get five?

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:08.730
So warm.

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:12.470
<i>On the battlefield, those who 
let their guard down die first,</i>

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:16.820
<i>but I have a sweet wife, good underlings,</i>

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:19.930
<i>good food and good drink.</i>

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:25.280
<i>Right now, I'd like to enjoy this happiness 
to the full extent as long as possible.</i>

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:31.290
Next up, we've got Nobu Plus.

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.020
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:38.270
Nobu's eel sure looked good.

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:43.020
<b>Morishita</b>

00:10:38.270 --> 00:10:38.990
It sure did!

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:43.010
Anyway, the place we've come 
to here is called Morishita.

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:45.500
Over here we've got the Takabashi 
shopping district and

00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:48.840
<b>Kenichi Nagira</b>

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:48.850
the Noraku Michi, otherwise 
known as Noraku Road.

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:52.280
This is Shitamachi. And if you 
say Shitamachi, it means eel.

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:53.790
And if you say eel, it means Nagira.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:54.690
Huh? I've never heard of that before.

00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:57.210
I really hope that place is still open.

00:10:57.210 --> 00:10:58.350
Let's go already.

00:10:58.350 --> 00:10:59.310
It's this way.

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:04.870
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:02.750
Kenichi Nagira is going to go around the bars

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:06.450
here to find the amazing 
dishes featured in "Nobu."

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:07.360
<b>Kenichi Nagira's search for the "Nobu" bar</b>

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:09.320
Here it is, here it is. We're finally here.

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:11.250
It's called "Torichou."

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:12.480
They're a yakitori place.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:13.620
Yakitori?

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:17.300
<b>Kenichi Nagira
 Born in Tokyo's Ginza. Made his debut in 1970 as a folk singer.
 Since then, he's been active as an actor, celebrity, essayist.
 Has been in multiple shows that take place in bars or Shitamachi</b>

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:15.040
You're wondering why we're not 
going to an eel restaurant.

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:18.290
Sure, if we go to a place that 
specializes in eel, we can order eel.

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:21.290
<b>Yakitori</b>

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:37.150
<b>Morishita 

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:21.300
But specifically going 
somewhere else is the trick.

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:22.220
Let's go in.

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:23.650
That's our Nagira-san.

00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:24.590
Hello.

00:11:24.590 --> 00:11:26.060
Welcome!

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:27.270
So lively!

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:29.280
What a voice!

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:30.110
It really carries, doesn't it.

00:11:30.110 --> 00:11:31.470
It's been a while.

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:35.570
Torichou is a cozy restaurant 
where you can enjoy

00:11:32.510 --> 00:11:37.150
<b>Sumibi Yakitori Unagi   Izakaya Torichou</b>

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:37.170
some real home cooking.

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:41.480
<b>Torichou
Master, Ishida Masaki-san</b>

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:39.450
I came to have some eel.

00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:40.200
Sounds good.

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:43.110
We're starting with live fish, so 
it'll take twenty, thirty minutes.

00:11:41.510 --> 00:13:29.090
<b>Morishita 

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:43.800
Is that okay?

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:45.470
Waiting for the eel to
cook is also key.

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:47.680
While I wait, Tosazukuri-style bonito?

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:49.410
Sounds good.
So I should bring that?

00:11:47.670 --> 00:11:49.170
Yes.

00:11:49.170 --> 00:11:49.680
Sure.

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:53.310
While the head chef
is grilling the eel...

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:57.730
<b>Torichou   Miku-san</b>

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.000
Thank you for waiting.

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:55.000
Thank you.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:57.740
One Tosazukuri-style 
bonito and a draft beer.

00:11:57.740 --> 00:11:59.750
If you walk slowly, you'll 
be on camera longer.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:00.700
Got it.

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:01.970
So cute.

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:06.910
Why don't we wait a little bit?

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:09.050
They're getting done!
They're getting done!

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:14.080
The grill marks, the shine, 
the scent is all amazing.

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:18.550
This is a classic izakaya 
fit for Shitamachi.

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:19.970
It sure is!

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:21.830
Who am I talking to?

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:23.360
Hey, to me, to me!

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:24.530
I was talking to myself.

00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:25.690
You're obnoxious.

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:27.760
Look, they're already done!

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:29.050
What do you insist on, head chef?

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:32.590
Well, it's that they're domestic fish.

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:33.860
They can come from abroad, huh?

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:34.370
That's right.

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:35.880
Even eel. Even eel, heh.

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:37.490
That's right.

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:39.460
Stop messing with the chef.

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:41.930
"Edomae" was the designation 
to be used for eel that was

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:45.840
fished out of the waterway in front of 
Edo, meaning in front of the Edo Castle.

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:50.410
After that, whatever they caught they 
started to call Edomae, even if was

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:55.450
from Tokyo Bay, but anyway, eel 
was the origin for that moniker.

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:53.200
That's right.

00:12:55.460 --> 00:13:01.760
Enough with the trivia. Try it!
I really want to know what it's like.

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:04.220
That was a good bite.

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:05.210
It's so tender.

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:06.840
It's fluffy.

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:11.710
The eel falls apart by itself.

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:12.940
I know what you mean!

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:15.740
And nothing goes with eel like sake!

00:13:17.140 --> 00:13:19.990
I need everyone from Izakaya 
Nobu to come over here.

00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:22.070
I'm here. That should be enough.

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:26.740
Even Nagira-san approves of "Sumibi 
Yakitori Unagi, Izakaya Torichou".

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:29.090
<b>Assistance: Gurunabi                                 To be continued</b>

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:28.660
It's a five minute walk from 
the Morishita station.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:32.190
If you want delicious chicken 
and eel, come here, come here!

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:58.010
<b>Next Time...
A Tempura Early Summer Mix</b>

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:54.170
Next time on "Isekai Izakaya"
aka "Izakaya Nobu in Aitheria."

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:57.500
Please sample the tasty tales.
